# The standard-library files libRuntime is made of (owner, 2026-11-03):
# built once per target with `xcc --emit-runtime Par.xc` and linked
# dynamically by every program for that target; a program then skips their
# source. One name per line, as it appears in an #import.
#
# Not ParSoftFloat.xc: a GPU kernel inlines its functions' bodies (the
# correctly rounded division and square root of an accuracy block), so a
# program compiles it as source — it comes as one of the library's
# stdImports.
Par.xc
ParDevice.xc
ParWorker.xc
ParMetal.xc
ParVulkan.xc
ParCuda.xc
ParRemote.xc
ParTiles.xc
ParWebGpu.xc
Mdns.xc
